{"type":"cards","design":"P66_CARDS_2X2","title":"Governed self-service analytics in Looker","lead":"Looker's semantic layer ensures every merchandising and store team queries the exact same metric definitions.","items":[{"title":"Version-controlled LookML metrics","text":"Centralized Git-backed LookML models codify net sales, gross margin, and sell-through calculations once so every department queries identical logic.","icon":"code-refresh"},{"title":"Role-based store dashboards","text":"Row-level access filters tailor operational views automatically so store managers see local register performance while regional directors compare territories.","icon":"user-hub"},{"title":"Cross-channel margin visibility","text":"Unified explores join digital shopping carts with physical store fulfillment costs to expose true omnichannel product profitability in real time.","icon":"cloud-layers"},{"title":"Scheduled stockout anomaly alerts","text":"Automated threshold checks monitor high-velocity items and notify allocation planners via email or chat when shelf quantities drop below safety levels.","icon":"hex-bolt"}],"callout":{"text":"Governing metrics in a semantic layer eliminates conflicting spreadsheet formulas across merchandising, finance, and store operations."},"notes":"Looker sits directly on top of our governed warehouse to provide a single version-controlled LookML semantic layer. Store managers, merchandisers, and finance analysts interact with role-based dashboards and automated stockout alerts without exporting data into spreadsheets.

